# ---- Model backend defaults ----
#
# THESE DO NOT APPLY TO A CONFIGURED TIER. `BackendConfig.from_env(prefix=...)` builds a
# subclass whose settings config is REPLACED rather than merged, so a tier reads only its
# own `PERSONA_<TIER>_*` names. Setting PERSONA_MAX_TOKENS=32000 leaves the mid tier on the
# 4096 default, silently — there is no warning, and the value simply never arrives.
#
# So these are defaults for the UNTIERED path. To change a tier, set its own copy:
#   PERSONA_FRONTIER_MAX_TOKENS / PERSONA_MID_MAX_TOKENS / PERSONA_SMALL_MAX_TOKENS
#   PERSONA_FRONTIER_TEMPERATURE / PERSONA_MID_TEMPERATURE / PERSONA_SMALL_TEMPERATURE
#   ...and the same prefixing for EXTRA_BODY, REQUEST_TIMEOUT_S, BASE_URL, TOP_P.
# Those per-tier names work and are pinned by a test; they were simply never written down.
# Documented 2026-09-16 after a sweep found the replacement semantics undocumented.
#PERSONA_EXTRA_BODY=
#PERSONA_MAX_TOKENS=4096
#PERSONA_TEMPERATURE=0.0
# Per-tier equivalents (uncomment the ones you actually need):
#PERSONA_FRONTIER_MAX_TOKENS=
#PERSONA_MID_MAX_TOKENS=
#PERSONA_SMALL_MAX_TOKENS=
#PERSONA_FRONTIER_TEMPERATURE=
#PERSONA_MID_TEMPERATURE=
#PERSONA_SMALL_TEMPERATURE=

